## 🔬 Research Overview

This division explores robotics, electronics, mechanical systems, automation, and intelligent machines.

The goal is to understand how machines are designed, built, controlled, and integrated with intelligent software.

## ⚙️ Research Areas

| Field | Focus |
|---|---|
| 🤖 Robotics | Robot design and control |
| ⚡ Electronics | Circuits and electronic systems |
| 🦾 Mechanical Engineering | Mechanisms and motion |
| 🧠 Robot Intelligence | AI-powered robotics |
| 🎛️ Automation | Automated systems and control |
| 🔌 Embedded Systems | Microcontrollers and sensors |
| 📡 Sensors & Actuators | Sensing and physical interaction |

## 🎯 Research Objectives

- Understand the fundamentals of robotics and engineering.
- Learn electronic circuits and embedded systems.
- Explore sensors, motors, and microcontrollers.
- Develop basic robotic prototypes.
- Experiment with automation and intelligent control.
- Combine AI with physical machines.

## 🧪 Engineering Experiments

Practical experiments and prototypes will be documented here.

Each experiment should include:
- Objective
- Required components
- Design and methodology
- Implementation
- Observations and results
- Problems and improvements

## 🛠️ Technologies & Tools

- Python
